      "outcome": {
        "identical": true,
        "text": "## Quoting the request id\n\nEvery API response carries `X-Candle-Request-Id` (browsers can read it; CORS exposes it). When you report a failed trade or any other failed call, quote that id: it is on the request's `[AgentRequest]` and error log lines, so it finds the exact one. `CandleApiError.requestId` in the SDK holds it, and the error message ends with `(request id <id>)`. You may send your own `X-Candle-Request-Id` (8 to 64 characters from `A-Za-z0-9._-`); anything else is replaced."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "docs-sdk-changelog",
      "scenario": "docs",
      "args": {
        "file": "packages/sdk/CHANGELOG.md"
      },
      "outcome": {
        "entry": "Release 0.6.38 (BE-4297); it carries the 0.6.37 code, so it waits on the same 2026-11-24T09:00Z gate, for an API that sends `X-Candle-Request-Id` in production. `CandleApiError.requestId` keeps the API's `X-Candle-Request-Id` from the failed response (also from a non-envelope `HTTP_<status>` answer), and the error message ends with `(request id <id>)`; quote it when reporting a failed call. Absent from an older API. `REQUEST_ID_HEADER` and `requestIdOf(response)` are exported. No request or route changes. A `failed` or `timeout` outcome from `submitAtomicLaunch()` carries `requestId` when the submit response sent one, and the `JITO_BUNDLE_*` error `selfLaunch()` builds from it keeps it; token-page and holder-exit errors keep it too."
      }
    }
